{{Politics of Okaiken}}

The '''Leader of the Opposition''' of [[Okaiken]] is the leader of the largest political party in the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken|House of Commoners]] that is not in government. The office was formally established on 22 December 1885, following the promulgation of the Diet Law during the [[Saito Restoration]].

The current Leader of the Opposition is [[Koichiro Sadanuma]] of the [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Liberal Democratic Party]], who has served since 28 October 2025 following his election as LDP President and the party's surge in the [[Okaiken general election, 2025|2025 general election]].

==List of Leaders of the Opposition==
The following is a list of Leaders of the Opposition since the office's formal establishment in 1885. The office was suspended from 1940 to 1953 during the [[Imperial Rule Assistance Association|Taisei Yokusankai]] era and subsequent post-war reconstruction.

===1885–1940: Early constitutional period===
The early constitutional period saw opposition leadership shift between the {{nihongo|Kenseitō|憲政党|Constitutional Party}} and {{nihongo|Rikken Seiyūkai|立憲政友会}}, with the position often complicated by the existence of multiple opposition parties and the dominance of non-party or military cabinets.

