===1940–1953: Suspension of the office===
The office of Leader of the Opposition was effectively suspended following the dissolution of political parties into the [[Imperial Rule Assistance Association|Taisei Yokusankai]] in 1940. The one-party state eliminated organised opposition, and the role ceased to function until its restoration under post-occupation constitutional reforms in 1953.

===1953–1968: Post-war period===
Following the restoration of multi-party democracy in 1953, the opposition leadership has been held by leaders of the major non-governing parties, primarily the [[Progressive Party of Okaiken|Progressive Party]] during periods of [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|LDP]] dominance, and vice versa.

